const NARRATED_AUDIO_CUES={"a":[{"start":4.0,"end":7.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Well five six seven eight nine ten eleven twelve now"},{"start":9.0,"end":11.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"say something in there tell"},{"start":13.0,"end":15.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Testy testy one two three four yes."},{"start":15.0,"end":17.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"them what your name is okay"},{"start":17.0,"end":17.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"My name is Jacques."},{"start":17.0,"end":26.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"fine now at that point now push the stop button stop see stop just push that"},{"start":34.0,"end":36.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Push that button down. Testing one,"},{"start":36.0,"end":38.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"two, three, four. Testing one, two, three, four."},{"start":39.0,"end":40.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Testing one, two, three, four."},{"start":214.0,"end":218.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I'll just, yeah, I don't know if this thing works right."},{"start":220.0,"end":221.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Yes, we left in,"},{"start":222.0,"end":223.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we left"},{"start":227.0,"end":240.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we left (Location, sounded like \"Aviaire\"), we left in May and went to Strasbourg and there we had a show of our penny postcards that we got to come to Strasbourg to be induced in the service."},{"start":241.0,"end":253.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"As a first-class brick (Possibly \"pick\", this word is slurred), we always we went together assembled and we went up to to Germany in the Polish border."},{"start":255.0,"end":257.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"When we got there at the Polish border,"},{"start":257.0,"end":258.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"gee,"},{"start":258.0,"end":261.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"it was as cold we was all freezing we do it with our summer clothes."},{"start":262.0,"end":265.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now there we had six months training."},{"start":266.0,"end":275.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"After six weeks, only quite six months, it became a bit rain from May till October."},{"start":275.0,"end":277.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In October we went, we"},{"start":278.0,"end":286.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"were sent, we went to the railroad station at one evening and drove all night,"},{"start":286.0,"end":291.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and then next morning we was in Tilsit."},{"start":293.0,"end":295.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In Tilsit (modern day Sovetsk) in East Germany,"},{"start":296.0,"end":299.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and there we have stayed for two days."},{"start":300.0,"end":304.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"On the third day we went on a ship,"},{"start":304.0,"end":309.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"the Mamel, and we were there overnight, we was on that boat."},{"start":310.0,"end":312.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And from that on,"},{"start":313.0,"end":317.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"then we was on a little small gauge railroad."},{"start":318.0,"end":322.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Open cars and we rode there all day,"},{"start":322.0,"end":326.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but it was really cold yet already."},{"start":326.0,"end":335.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The cold was already there in October and we was afraid this thing is going to collapse when it went over those bridges."},{"start":336.0,"end":338.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It was all rickety-rackety."},{"start":341.0,"end":343.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then up we went."},{"start":343.0,"end":345.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Up the hill, on there,"},{"start":345.0,"end":349.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"march and march and march. We marched in for two,"},{"start":349.0,"end":358.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"three days till we got in a little village and there we stayed overnight in the barns, little stables,"},{"start":358.0,"end":360.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"what we could find to sleep on."},{"start":361.0,"end":368.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And next morning we went and walked again for a day, half a day, and then we reached the trenches."},{"start":369.0,"end":371.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I wanted to wash near the back of the trenches."},{"start":373.0,"end":378.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So there we had the first, that was the soup kitchen there,"},{"start":378.0,"end":381.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and we had the first hot meal on our trip."},{"start":384.0,"end":388.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So then all of a sudden the Russians start shooting at us."},{"start":389.0,"end":398.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then when the order came, dig in, so we had all a big shovel (this sounds like slurred \"shagun\", maybe shotgun or shovel), everyone had to dig a hole to get down inside."},{"start":399.0,"end":412.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then the next morning we got further ahead and there were some trenches and in the trenches were some holes where you could sleep in it, you lay down in those trenches."},{"start":414.0,"end":422.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we stayed in those trenches for a week, two hours on and two hours off on the watch."},{"start":423.0,"end":432.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then we came back for a week and rested there and at that week we rested,"},{"start":433.0,"end":440.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but in the daytime we had to go from the front and dig some more trenches."},{"start":442.0,"end":456.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But in the meantime then it got cold, it got really cold. But we still managed with our clothes on and sleeping in the barn and a little bit of straw, you know."},{"start":458.0,"end":466.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So all of a sudden the order came we have to move. We moved I is so far right away where we moved."},{"start":467.0,"end":477.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We moved, we don't know the names of the villages we passed, then we stopped in one village and there was a person,"},{"start":478.0,"end":480.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"the commandant he tells us,"},{"start":481.0,"end":483.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"one group gets in this barn,"},{"start":483.0,"end":486.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"the other group gets in this barn and so we slept there overnight."},{"start":487.0,"end":490.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Next morning they had coffee and bread."},{"start":492.0,"end":494.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then start marching again."},{"start":495.0,"end":497.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we marched again,"},{"start":497.0,"end":505.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and this time we *really* heard the shooting going on in the front. It was close by."},{"start":506.0,"end":517.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So it was kind of a little bit eerie should we go a little further (he chuckles here with the attitude of \"it would be really funny if we stopped\"), but we had to go we couldn't stop it. So we marched again and all of a sudden we heard some shooting at us"},{"start":518.0,"end":529.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and there was a group of budgeteers ( pronounced ba-je-tes) that came right next to us in the meadows there. We was on the road and they came in the meadows."},{"start":529.0,"end":532.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And those that was on the road, my dear,"},{"start":532.0,"end":532.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"exploded."},{"start":533.0,"end":535.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then the order came,"},{"start":535.0,"end":543.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"march into the meadows. So we go down in the meadows and watch in the meadows and then the shooting stopped."},{"start":544.0,"end":545.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It was a watch till evening (it sounds like \"until we marched till evening\")."},{"start":546.0,"end":564.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In the evening then we was again in a little hamlet or what[ever] it was, I don't know, and there [unknown word] was laying there for the day or two and after that it went into trenches."},{"start":565.0,"end":573.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Not that trenches was not too bad, but really they called [Indecipherable]. There was where I got start freezing and very,"},{"start":573.0,"end":574.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"very cold."},{"start":575.0,"end":585.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But we didn't [mind] the cold so much as the rain. When it started, thin rain was alright, but when it rained it was wet, you know, and everything was cold and wet."},{"start":586.0,"end":591.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The food came regularly then in the evening. In the evening we [were] getting a hot meal."},{"start":591.0,"end":597.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But during the day we just had to chew on a piece of bread if we have one left from coffee,"},{"start":597.0,"end":597.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"you know."},{"start":600.0,"end":614.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we was all winter there in Russia, on and off in the trenches and dug in trenches and that trench digging was very, very tough because the front, the ground was [not only] frozen or but..."},{"start":615.0,"end":635.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"[also] Deep -- one metre deep was the ground frozen. So we had uh we had a thicker [indecipherable] that we get down there. Then when we was down one metre deep then the wind didn't hit us no more, so we took down in and it was nice when the wind didn't hit us, the wind went over, so it was nice and warm down there."},{"start":637.0,"end":637.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Uh"},{"start":639.0,"end":640.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"so"},{"start":641.0,"end":651.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In the beginning we had nothing much to do there, just talking and sleeping and things, there was not much uh of anything."},{"start":652.0,"end":665.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Only we found a potato field where the potato was frozen. And there we went there and dug the frozen potato out and we cooked them potatoes."},{"start":666.0,"end":675.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So, unfortunately we could catch something from the Russian farmers when in the evening when nobody,"},{"start":675.0,"end":682.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"when it gets dark. So we went around looking for the Russian farmers and sometimes you get a piece of bread,"},{"start":682.0,"end":690.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"you know, to get a piece of bread. Well, it was pretty good, are we? We put it alone all winter. Then when the spring came..."},{"start":693.0,"end":696.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We were transferred to Galicia."},{"start":697.0,"end":706.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The order came to go down to Galicia. There was a big offensive, the Russians started the offensive in Galicia and we had to go down there."},{"start":706.0,"end":715.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"That took about two or three days in those boxcars, you know, 48 men and eight horses in those cars we went in there."},{"start":716.0,"end":718.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It was not a pleasant trip."},{"start":719.0,"end":720.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"When one village,"},{"start":720.0,"end":730.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they stopped there for an hour or two hours, and there came some soldiers,"},{"start":730.0,"end":733.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they came there and they had some hot soup for us."},{"start":734.0,"end":744.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But you should have seen that soup, it was as black as coal and no taste whatsoever but you swallowed it because it was warm, you had something warm in your stomach."},{"start":745.0,"end":749.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And you had a piece of bread left from that breakfast,"},{"start":749.0,"end":755.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"so that was pretty good. So we got and there we get near another piece of bread for the evening."},{"start":758.0,"end":764.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And by next day, by next morning then we was in Galicia, we get into mountains,"},{"start":764.0,"end":769.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we get into railroad cars, but"},{"start":770.0,"end":779.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The one car pushed and the other car pulled, so when it went around the bend, the short bend,"},{"start":779.0,"end":794.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they give the signals, the railroads give the signals, that he should stop pushing or the other one should pull and so that went up for about all morning."},{"start":794.0,"end":802.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Push and pull, push and pull, it was so slow you could walk faster than we went up that hill in the mountains."},{"start":802.0,"end":803.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But we went up there,"},{"start":803.0,"end":803.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but when we,"},{"start":803.0,"end":810.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"once we was up there then what was alright, the Russians were shooting at us, but"},{"start":811.0,"end":822.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"They missed us. They went, they shot above because we was behind the mountains and the projectiles, they should right before right over the mountains in the back of [us] (the words \"back of\" sounds like \"bagel\"). So we was not to be there."},{"start":826.0,"end":829.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then all of a sudden there come the order we should attack."},{"start":830.0,"end":855.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we're going to attack, yeah we're going to attack, *sure* (said sarcastically, or almost reluctantly) we get out of our trenches and go into front but we did not there was nobody to lead us we just run around wild in the cornfield - there was cornfields there -  we all around in the cornfields and duck here and duck there and all of a sudden then the order came we should pull back so we pulled back again"},{"start":856.0,"end":864.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And we was in the trenches and we went in the trenches and what happened in on the other side in the same trenches was the Russians."},{"start":865.0,"end":880.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So there was quite a kind of confusion and then we we pulled back around the other way within the trenches we around the other way and then out of the trenches and run back again."},{"start":882.0,"end":884.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So then we reached the little woods."},{"start":884.0,"end":892.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then we was in the woods and there we had then we collect us all together and there we lay there and waited for orders"},{"start":893.0,"end":895.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but orders never came."},{"start":895.0,"end":904.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So all of a sudden the lieutenant he collect us and says now we have to march ahead."},{"start":905.0,"end":906.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Well, when we started marching ahead,"},{"start":906.0,"end":911.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"then the Russians started with the highway artillery."},{"start":912.0,"end":914.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we went back."},{"start":915.0,"end":920.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We went back again in the trenches and then the lieutenant said,"},{"start":921.0,"end":925.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"now he needs a couple of men."},{"start":925.0,"end":932.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"To play in between the [undecipherable] back trenches and the front trenches to get the orders back and forward."},{"start":933.0,"end":946.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now nobody was volunteering, so he picked me and he picked another guy and there was tight (instead of tight, I think he meant to say \"right there\") an apple orchard. I laid in an apple orchard and the other guy went about"},{"start":947.0,"end":969.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"fifty feet, fifty feet ahead, and lay down there in the thing and then he said we \"dug in\". I dug in about three two feet or something like that and dug in there and lay there and waited for orders we got orders and no orders ever came, no orders,  but all of a sudden there was a a fifteen centimeter"},{"start":970.0,"end":979.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"projectile that came down through the [tree?] (shounds like \"ah-be-glee\") and landed right next to me. It was as tall as I am and boy that did I run."},{"start":980.0,"end":987.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I just run back in the trench and let nobody bother me and I went back in the trench to the other guys."},{"start":987.0,"end":988.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And they asked me what happened."},{"start":988.0,"end":989.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I said \"gee God,"},{"start":989.0,"end":993.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that stuff was too much.\" But the projectiles didn't explode!"},{"start":994.0,"end":995.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"That was one lucky thing for me."},{"start":997.0,"end":1020.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so we laid there and for a couple of days and then one evening when we [undecipherable] we get out of the trenches and we lay under those apple trees there under the orchard and [we realized that we should] not be waiting for the soup to arrive, that the food should have come."},{"start":1021.0,"end":1045.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"One night I went to get the food, the next night somebody else get the food for the front, carried the kettles for the thing and after we was finished eating we laid around and waited and that's where I got wounded. during the night. All of a sudden I get a bullet in my chest and so I..."},{"start":1046.0,"end":1065.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"the fellas carried me back into trench and waited for the wagon to come. There a little wagon came with two little ponies and they put me on that wagon and they carried me back to the hospital, the wagon carrying me back to the hospital."},{"start":1066.0,"end":1068.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In the hospital then they"},{"start":1069.0,"end":1073.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Oh I don't know. I was two or three days in the hospital before a doctor examined me."},{"start":1074.0,"end":1076.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I don't know why what happened. I had no idea."},{"start":1077.0,"end":1085.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But the nurses looked at me, one nurse looked at me and there was Catholic sisters, they looked at me and she says \"oh that's alright\" (said very matter-of-factly)."},{"start":1086.0,"end":1092.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"Goodbye, lay down\". And so her that the doctor, she was that a doctor, maybe it wasn't much,"},{"start":1092.0,"end":1094.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"was just a little scratch, I don't know."},{"start":1094.0,"end":1120.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so the doctor came two or three days later and he examined me and then he put me on the next train load that went into the country- back to Germany and then he put me on that train and I [went] to Schlesien in Germany in a hospital there."},{"start":1121.0,"end":1125.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So I was there in hospital for a couple of weeks and the"},{"start":1127.0,"end":1129.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"doctors said nothing,"},{"start":1129.0,"end":1142.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they didn't say about an operation or anything and so they transferred me from that hospital into another hospital in Marienburg."},{"start":1145.0,"end":1147.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that was in Germany, not in Poland,"},{"start":1147.0,"end":1148.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but in Marienburg."},{"start":1149.0,"end":1154.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And there I was in the hospital and all of a sudden a doctor came to examine me."},{"start":1155.0,"end":1157.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And he says, \"where are you from?\""},{"start":1158.0,"end":1159.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And I said, \"from Strasbourg.\""},{"start":1159.0,"end":1160.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"Oh,\""},{"start":1160.0,"end":1160.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"he said,"},{"start":1160.0,"end":1161.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"Strasbourg,"},{"start":1161.0,"end":1162.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that's where I come from.\""},{"start":1162.0,"end":1165.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then he said, \"is that what happened?\""},{"start":1165.0,"end":1168.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So I said, what happened to you? Then I told him."},{"start":1168.0,"end":1187.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then he says, uh, can you look the other one that has had x-rays taken? And then he says, \"that it's alright, you're you're going to be alright. But don't let anybody operate on you, because your wound is very nice healed. The lung is healed."},{"start":1188.0,"end":1189.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And the lung is nice to heal, but if they want to operate to get it out"},{"start":1192.0,"end":1200.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they might cut more of the lung and then it might not heal as nice. So just forget about it. It's not heavy. It's only about nine gram."},{"start":1202.0,"end":1204.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So be good now and uh"},{"start":1205.0,"end":1208.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"till we see you again.\" (Auf Weider Sen)"},{"start":1209.0,"end":1227.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So I was there in that hospital for a couple of weeks and till one day they came and picked me up and sent me in back to the regiment where I came from in Silesia."},{"start":1229.0,"end":1238.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"That was the recuperation company and then I could walk around and we"},{"start":1241.0,"end":1247.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"had a nice time there, we had nothing to do, you know, we had regular coffee for breakfast, yeah,"},{"start":1248.0,"end":1256.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and soup for lunch and a cold piece of bread and a little sausage or a herring or something for dinner."},{"start":1257.0,"end":1260.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The West had nice water to drink, you know, it was nice, yeah."},{"start":1269.0,"end":1280.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The worst thing was the trip from Russia to Austria, to the, to the mountains there. And we was"},{"start":1282.0,"end":1299.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But in box cars, and those cars was closed up and just a little bit of hole for the air to come in for all all and such those box cars what you call them in this country, eight horses and forty eight men."},{"start":1300.0,"end":1306.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And they stopped maybe every six hours, eight hours."},{"start":1307.0,"end":1309.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"They stopped on a railroad station,"},{"start":1309.0,"end":1311.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"where we could get out for a while,"},{"start":1311.0,"end":1312.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"stretch our legs."},{"start":1314.0,"end":1318.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then when we were at our destination,"},{"start":1320.0,"end":1322.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"where that was I don't know,"},{"start":1322.0,"end":1328.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but it was just on a railroad station out of the town,"},{"start":1328.0,"end":1330.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"somewhere in there."},{"start":1331.0,"end":1338.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then we went from her, then we marched up, uphill till"},{"start":1339.0,"end":1347.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"oh so, there a nice village was up there on the hill, but half of the village was destroyed."},{"start":1348.0,"end":1353.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And the people, the houses that stand was very nicely kept, you could see that."},{"start":1355.0,"end":1378.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so but we had to sleep outside the village in the trench or in the grass where we were laying there for the night. Then in the morning we get our coffee as we -  usually we send somebody in the back and get some coffee - and and the Russian was not shooting at us. They must have [different] things."},{"start":1381.0,"end":1406.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now, next day, then we start marching again and there we had a close by, then we was close by to the front and we was behind a mountain but the Russians was shooting at us but they had to shoot over us because if they shoot short"},{"start":1407.0,"end":1417.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they hit a mountain, if they shoot over the mountain, then they didn't hit us. So we was pretty safe there, was lucky there, we laid there for a whole day."},{"start":1418.0,"end":1426.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But the next day, next day has to go advance again. And that..."},{"start":1426.0,"end":1431.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"That was a little bit of a hassle after it's gone. We went through the beet fields,"},{"start":1431.0,"end":1432.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"look,"},{"start":1433.0,"end":1436.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"running in the beet fields and the right and left, and nobody,"},{"start":1436.0,"end":1446.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I don't know, nobody knows where he was going and all of a sudden that we was in a trench. We jumped in the trench,"},{"start":1446.0,"end":1449.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"all of us we jumped in the trench there and"},{"start":1450.0,"end":1454.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then by evening when we when we when the evening came"},{"start":1456.0,"end":1464.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there on on one side in the trench and one side of the trench was the Russian and we was in the same trench and we was on the other side of the trench."},{"start":1466.0,"end":1474.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But nobody bothered, we just uh kept quiet because everybody was we don't know, we had no orders or nothing, so"},{"start":1474.0,"end":1481.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"When the night comes we packed out and we went back, we pulled back."},{"start":1481.0,"end":1494.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And we laid in the back there in the in a village in a in a orchard next to a village. Um there"},{"start":1495.0,"end":1504.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The Russians they found us, they start shooting with heavy artillery at us from far. And then we"},{"start":1507.0,"end":1518.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"had to dig some foxholes and each one laid in the foxhole, dig down as much as just that you fit in the foxhole, there we laid in the foxhole."},{"start":1522.0,"end":1530.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The Russians with the artillery have shortened, not heavy, but uh then and when there came one, a there come a big fellow over and"},{"start":1531.0,"end":1534.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I laid in the foxhole on under a apple tree."},{"start":1536.0,"end":1546.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And uh I have I heard that noise in the apple tree *zhooom* and there was a [projectile]"},{"start":1547.0,"end":1571.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"about 15 cm (i think he means to say about \"15 centimeters away from me\") and he didn't explode, he (the bomb) was laying right next to me in the trench. The point looked into my trench where I was laying. I looked around and looked at this thing and lost my breath but up I went and run back! (he says this with a chuckle, almost like giddiness of not being dead)"},{"start":1572.0,"end":1596.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"From there I run further back in the where the other fellows was. surely, nobody said anything. I was laying there then the next day with the other fellows. next day it was quiet no action, no shooting here and there, we heard no guns and all that but"},{"start":1597.0,"end":1600.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"At night we laid in"},{"start":1602.0,"end":1606.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"a little, a little uh what you call a little"},{"start":1609.0,"end":1618.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"forest. It was not exactly a forest, it was just a big bush, I suppose, I don't know. And there we was waiting for the the dinner to come."},{"start":1619.0,"end":1622.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And while we was waiting to for the dinner to come front, you know."},{"start":1623.0,"end":1625.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"There I got wounded,"},{"start":1626.0,"end":1630.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and there they packed me up and sent me back to the hospital."},{"start":1632.0,"end":1633.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And,"},{"start":1633.0,"end":1634.0,"speaker":"Speaker C","text":"Did it hurt? (Gillian)"},{"start":1634.0,"end":1634.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"hmm?"},{"start":1634.0,"end":1636.0,"speaker":"Speaker C","text":"Did it hurt?"},{"start":1637.0,"end":1638.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Yeah, it hurt a little."},{"start":1639.0,"end":1645.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then be back to the hospital. There I was in the hospital for two days, or three days,"},{"start":1645.0,"end":1647.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and then they sent us back"},{"start":1648.0,"end":1661.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"to the in the German Hospital, Silesia, a nurse, and there I was examined by the doctors, more doctors examined and they look around and"},{"start":1662.0,"end":1672.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"they didn't say nothing, they say \"alright, they didn't\" they just looked at it and said they heard that now then they"},{"start":1675.0,"end":1679.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"No, but she (the bullet) had travelled, there should be the bullet went in here. (he is now pointing at his chest)"},{"start":1680.0,"end":1680.0,"speaker":"Speaker E","text":"Which has?"},{"start":1681.0,"end":1682.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Yeah, you ca"},{"start":1682.0,"end":1684.0,"speaker":"Speaker E","text":"Tell me, say \"in there\"."},{"start":1684.0,"end":1684.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Yeah."},{"start":1684.0,"end":1687.0,"speaker":"Speaker E","text":"Say in there. Describe it."},{"start":1688.0,"end":1693.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"the second button up from the coat."},{"start":1694.0,"end":1707.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there came the bullet, right down in and in my chest. No, it wasn't. When it struck it skipped right over the lung. He (the bullet) didn't hit the heart, he didn't reach the heart, was going slow I suppose,"},{"start":1707.0,"end":1707.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I don't know."},{"start":1709.0,"end":1715.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So, when I was in that hospital and the"},{"start":1716.0,"end":1718.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"They know what to do with me, I suppose,"},{"start":1718.0,"end":1730.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and so they sent me back to another hospital. And from that other hospital the doctor said if I want to be operated on, they can operate,"},{"start":1730.0,"end":1737.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but it's not, they don't know, they have not the thing, they didn't force that."},{"start":1738.0,"end":1739.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So I..."},{"start":1741.0,"end":1758.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"didn't show nothing. on that healed up and when I was healed didn't send nothing no more they just sent me back to the to the other army and there I got sick. now one day I got sick I spit blood"},{"start":1763.0,"end":1766.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"then I went to the hospital in Marienburg"},{"start":1769.0,"end":1790.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In Marianberg was a nice hospital, a Catholic sisters was a temple in the hospital and it was very nice and all of a sudden comes a doctor in and charming me then he says where do you come from and I say \"from Alsace\"."},{"start":1791.0,"end":1792.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"He says, \"oh\","},{"start":1792.0,"end":1795.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"I come from Alsace too, I come from Strasbourg!\""},{"start":1796.0,"end":1796.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Oh, I say, \"oh,"},{"start":1796.0,"end":1799.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I was working in Strasbourg by Resto Wallander.\""},{"start":1799.0,"end":1800.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"He says,"},{"start":1800.0,"end":1800.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"oh,"},{"start":1800.0,"end":1801.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that's a nice restaurant!\","},{"start":1801.0,"end":1802.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"I know\"."},{"start":1802.0,"end":1804.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"He says,\"now, now, what happened,"},{"start":1804.0,"end":1806.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"what happened?\""},{"start":1806.0,"end":1813.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I said, \"I've got wounded in the chest\". Then he said, \"oh,"},{"start":1813.0,"end":1813.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"let me see.\""},{"start":1814.0,"end":1815.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now, he looked at it."},{"start":1816.0,"end":1817.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And he says, \"does it hurt?\""},{"start":1817.0,"end":1819.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And I say,\" no, it doesn't hurt no more."},{"start":1820.0,"end":1825.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It's all right, no it doesn't hurt, nothing.\" And he says, now, he says, \"all right, we're going to take x-ray tomorrow."},{"start":1826.0,"end":1828.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so I will see you tomorrow.\""},{"start":1829.0,"end":1834.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now tomorrow we took that x-ray and he looked at it and he says, \"oh,"},{"start":1834.0,"end":1837.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that is wonderful healing\", he says."},{"start":1841.0,"end":1865.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"I don't think we need any operation. but in case somebody wants to operate on you, don't let them operate because when we open the lung again and take that bullet out that might not heal as good as this. that is perfectly healed. very nice. and the bullet is not heavy. you don't carry heavy on that one\""},{"start":1865.0,"end":1889.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"And it's a and it's a steel bullet if it was a copper bullet will be difference, but this is a steel. steel is not poisonous. So be happy with it and uh yeah alright.\" And and so I was there about another two weeks a week or two weeks and then I was sent out uh back to the company and recuperation company again and"},{"start":1891.0,"end":1915.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So that was laying the recursion company until August. In August I was then to come to order for twelve men to go to the farm, to help the farmers to bring the wheat in. Uh so, one two three four five twelve, you go. So we went to a farm"},{"start":1916.0,"end":1919.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"and help the farmer to bring the wheat in."},{"start":1921.0,"end":1934.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We slept in the barn and eat on the farm.  the food, it was not uh too bad, it was pretty good. Only there was too many flies around the soup."},{"start":1936.0,"end":1937.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"That's the clue."},{"start":1938.0,"end":1945.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Once in a while one did fall in the soup. Well what you're going to do? You just hope you have to throw them out, you know. (he has a good chuckle here)"},{"start":1948.0,"end":1952.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so we stayed there till the potato crop came."},{"start":1953.0,"end":1959.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then we started picking up the potato and then it got cold."},{"start":1960.0,"end":1962.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And we was glad when it got cold that the..."},{"start":1963.0,"end":1989.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We were that we could go home because it was too cold there on the farm picking up those cold potatoes. And we we managed. when we come home and we were sitting around there and waited and every couple of months we was examined again, we was ready to go to the front again. But I I did feel like going back in the front again."},{"start":1990.0,"end":2003.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So I was always more or less sick for my, I had pain in my chest and [un]till the war was over. And now it didn't last long. no more then."},{"start":2004.0,"end":2005.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Uh"},{"start":2007.0,"end":2014.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So when I when I came home then I when the war was over we was"},{"start":2015.0,"end":2030.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The Alsatians were separated right away from the from the German soldiers. We were separated on uh on a week later we was all sent home. The Germans they stay there and the Alsatians were sent home."},{"start":2031.0,"end":2036.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And we too it took us a day to go from uh Koenigsberg"},{"start":2038.0,"end":2051.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"To Strasbourg. A whole day, we was [on a] slow train, and no train and the train was changed, the train when we was in Berlin was laid over,"},{"start":2051.0,"end":2061.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we laid over in Berlin for a while, and then in in Wiesbaden in South Germany we was laid over for a while, the train did go no further."},{"start":2061.0,"end":2063.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there was no train to go to Strasbourg (Alsace)."},{"start":2064.0,"end":2079.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But then all of a sudden there was a train that went to Strasbourg and we piled all into the train and the train was packed with soldiers. And then in Strasbourg I found another train after I probably went home."},{"start":2080.0,"end":2086.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And I was home a day or two and then I went back to Strasbourg on..."},{"start":2089.0,"end":2092.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"When I came back, when I went back to Strasbourg,"},{"start":2092.0,"end":2101.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I meet the boss I was working for before the war, before I went into the service and he says to me,"},{"start":2101.0,"end":2114.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"what are you doing? roaming around doing nothing\" and I said \"I do nothing? I just come from the, from the-\", \"oh that is alright\" he says, \"tomorrow you going to go to work, come on tomorrow you go to work.\""},{"start":2115.0,"end":2132.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I said, \"tomorrow? I have no clothes with me, no nothing, I [have to] go home and get them\". He says, \"you come tomorrow\". And so I went home and get my clothes and next day I was working. And I was working two days when the Frenchmens march into Strasbourg."},{"start":2136.0,"end":2140.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"At 12 o'clock, 1 o'clock or 2 o'clock."},{"start":2140.0,"end":2144.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Double the restaurant was full of soldiers,"},{"start":2144.0,"end":2146.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there was no standing room anymore,"},{"start":2146.0,"end":2154.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we can be, we feed the people as they come in and I don't know who paid the bill,"},{"start":2154.0,"end":2156.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"who paid that, we put the food down,"},{"start":2157.0,"end":2164.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we get them food, them food. I never know any, I didn't see any bill passed for anything else, but they all eat and then"},{"start":2165.0,"end":2170.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The chef *de rang* (Possibly spelled Derrain), he sent me out to get the cake for a party he had there."},{"start":2171.0,"end":2181.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And I go out and got a big, big round chocolate cake, what[ever] it was. Just as I stepped into the dining room,"},{"start":2181.0,"end":2184.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there was the Frenchman, a French officer,"},{"start":2184.0,"end":2185.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"he took the cake and said,"},{"start":2185.0,"end":2185.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"hey boy,"},{"start":2186.0,"end":2186.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"give me that cake.\""},{"start":2188.0,"end":2190.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so he took the cake and..."},{"start":2190.0,"end":2196.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I don't know what, where is that? I went back in the kitchen, looked for another one. no!"},{"start":2196.0,"end":2197.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there was no more cake."},{"start":2197.0,"end":2216.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So I disappeared a little bit. I thought, \"I'll make [something for] myself. I was not afraid [of getting in trouble]. but everything was upside down! Nobody said anything (about his attendance) but the people had a good time. They all was drinking and singing and bringing (random -inging word used as filler)."},{"start":2217.0,"end":2219.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And eating what he could find."},{"start":2220.0,"end":2224.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The[y] was no out of the on the table and off the table."},{"start":2225.0,"end":2229.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So when the evening came then we had to clean up the whole mess."},{"start":2230.0,"end":2232.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And the boss says, \"ya know,"},{"start":2232.0,"end":2234.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"it was a good day anyway.\""},{"start":2235.0,"end":2237.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"You have to make no money but you had a good day, a good time."},{"start":2239.0,"end":2240.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then,"},{"start":2240.0,"end":2242.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but next day was."},{"start":2243.0,"end":2258.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Not a cleaning up, there was so much m- such a mess in the restaurant that and the girls the the girls that washed, the[y] washed the windows and the floors and the thing, they they were so glad it was over too."},{"start":2260.0,"end":2261.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now"},{"start":2264.0,"end":2265.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So"},{"start":2270.0,"end":2272.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we was"},{"start":2274.0,"end":2292.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"home from the exercise, we're cold, in a hurry, we was poured up to the barracks and kept the clay (possibly \"grey\") clothes for the front, [the other clothes were] thrown out of the window. and everybody had to pick out his clothes,"},{"start":2292.0,"end":2295.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"take his measurements and take his size."},{"start":2296.0,"end":2302.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then by seven o'clock we was already on the go."},{"start":2303.0,"end":2314.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we was marched to another barrack and there we was put together as all counted and all together and there we was slept together in one big barn."},{"start":2317.0,"end":2321.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Next morning we was marched to the railroad station."},{"start":2322.0,"end":2324.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"went up in"},{"start":2327.0,"end":2333.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"the boxcars and went all the way up into Tilsit."},{"start":2333.0,"end":2348.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In Tilsit we got out and laid (i think he meant to say \"stayed\") two days in a [undecipherable] there, an upbound [undecipherable] (pronounced \"cassan\"). For two days we waited there in Tilsit."},{"start":2348.0,"end":2364.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then we went on the boat. There was a boat laying there and with that boat we went for one day and one night into Russia."},{"start":2365.0,"end":2371.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And there it was snow, that was the first snow we had then. And"},{"start":2372.0,"end":2380.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And after the boat stopped, we got on small gauge railroad cars."},{"start":2382.0,"end":2400.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I opened railroad, opened railroad cars and on those railroad cars we went half a day on those little until [we were] into Russia's [territory/land]."},{"start":2402.0,"end":2426.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"where we were, nobody knows.  it was just in. going. going in. and then we loaded on then we was unloaded and started to march till it was dark. where it was dark we went in the Russian farms in the village there and everybody got"},{"start":2427.0,"end":2428.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"erm, laid in the barns, (as in they started to hide out in the barns)"},{"start":2429.0,"end":2435.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but I don't want to... we got something to eat, yeah, till next morning."},{"start":2435.0,"end":2440.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Next morning we got tea from the Russians,"},{"start":2440.0,"end":2444.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"or from where we got it. but the kitchen they had tea, they had no coffee! (he seems pretty annoyed by this)"},{"start":2444.0,"end":2449.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We got tea and that was a funny tasting tea, I will say that."},{"start":2450.0,"end":2452.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we marched again,"},{"start":2452.0,"end":2453.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we marched again."},{"start":2454.0,"end":2465.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And then it starts to snow and snow and the more it snows the worse gets the marching."},{"start":2471.0,"end":2478.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The roads get bad and we march and the roads get worse and soggy."},{"start":2480.0,"end":2482.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And we marched on."},{"start":2482.0,"end":2489.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"In evening we sat down and we waited for the kitchen to come, for something to eat. The kitchen came,"},{"start":2490.0,"end":2491.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"didn't come that night."},{"start":2492.0,"end":2498.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we didn't know, [we thought that] by the morning she's going to be there. So we had nothing to eat that night."},{"start":2499.0,"end":2506.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So next morning we were up, everybody go up and no kitchen [arrived]."},{"start":2507.0,"end":2530.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"\"So what we gonna eat now?\" so some fellas they want to make a fire and don't to make themselves some coffee or something and they wouldn't allow it! then they says \"no, it's too dangerous. the fires here in the houses is too dangerous\" so we had no kit, nothing to eat again for that day. so we marched"},{"start":2531.0,"end":2540.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And by evening, when they was again in a Russian village and nothing to eat."},{"start":2541.0,"end":2547.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we go around and take from our Russian farms what we could get, a piece of bread or a piece of fish."},{"start":2551.0,"end":2557.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"There was a butcher in the company. when he says, \"I'm going to get something to eat.\""},{"start":2558.0,"end":2560.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And he went into Russian,"},{"start":2560.0,"end":2567.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"at night he went to a Russian stable of what it was and then they get themselves a lamb."},{"start":2569.0,"end":2573.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And they killed the lamb and they had something to eat."},{"start":2581.0,"end":2582.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"The Russians..."},{"start":2583.0,"end":2592.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"people, they couldn't say nothing because what they there were so many soldiers, there was only a couple of Russians there, the man was gone, the women's was alone,"},{"start":2593.0,"end":2594.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"there were a couple of old men there,"},{"start":2597.0,"end":2599.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but I don't think that was fair."},{"start":2599.0,"end":2604.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that the poor Russians they needed, they were so poor they had not much to eat themselves,"},{"start":2604.0,"end":2605.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I could see that."},{"start":2610.0,"end":2613.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"[After reading a prompt from gillian] \"Where after then did you go?\""},{"start":2613.0,"end":2615.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Oh from there we went,"},{"start":2616.0,"end":2631.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"that we went in to a village Ratsievilevitskiewicz, and that was a big, estate,"},{"start":2632.0,"end":2633.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"a wonderful estate."},{"start":2634.0,"end":2643.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But we couldn't go in there because there was the artillery or somebody was there, they had all the horses there."},{"start":2643.0,"end":2646.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Big officers was in there and we couldn't get in there."},{"start":2646.0,"end":2653.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We watched them laying about a couple of miles outside there, we had to stay overnight."},{"start":2655.0,"end":2656.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But then in the evening,"},{"start":2656.0,"end":2661.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"in the evening it was full moon, we watched, we walked over the snow direct."},{"start":2662.0,"end":2675.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"no road, we just walked over the snow direct to that, to that camp there where the soldiers. and the soldiers they asked, [if] they (as in Jacques' company) had nothing, they said they have nothing, so they give us raw"},{"start":2677.0,"end":2678.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"sugar."},{"start":2679.0,"end":2683.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now each one can pick up a really can full of raw sugar."},{"start":2684.0,"end":2688.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"They said they fed the horses with raw sugar. They had lots of horses there."},{"start":2690.0,"end":2697.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And so we went back. in the morning, nothing to eat."},{"start":2698.0,"end":2700.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So [there] was a potato field."},{"start":2703.0,"end":2713.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We could see the weather, but there was a potato field there. they put the stick through the snow. The snow was not that heavy yet, but we could see the potatoes."},{"start":2713.0,"end":2717.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"So we start digging and yeah, that was potatoes,"},{"start":2717.0,"end":2719.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"but the potatoes was frozen already."},{"start":2720.0,"end":2721.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"They was frozen already,"},{"start":2721.0,"end":2722.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"so..."},{"start":2723.0,"end":2725.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"We took them out anyway and we cooked them."},{"start":2725.0,"end":2731.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"They was very, very good, they was sweet. They smelled very sweet, but they was good."},{"start":2732.0,"end":2744.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then the next afternoon we lay there for a week or half a week or something. Next day we went to the other side of the village"},{"start":2748.0,"end":2758.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"on the farm there. and there was a Russian woman and she did give me a piece of bacon."},{"start":2759.0,"end":2762.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I want to [give] some silver money but she wouldn't take it."},{"start":2763.0,"end":2773.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But she gave me a piece of bacon. She went home and cooked the bacon stuck [it] in the bag."},{"start":2774.0,"end":2780.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"[I] put it in the pot with the potatoes and cooked a little bit and then each one get his [share]"},{"start":2781.0,"end":2795.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"[I was with] two/three fellows, we was together, each one get a small piece. but that was something to eat anyway beside raw potatoes/cooked potatoes/cooked sweet potatoes. so then"},{"start":2798.0,"end":2799.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"we start marching again"},{"start":2800.0,"end":2801.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"And marching."},{"start":2802.0,"end":2803.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Then it starts to rain."},{"start":2804.0,"end":2810.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Rain and snowing, rain and snowing. The road was [eventually] just one sheet of ice."},{"start":2811.0,"end":2821.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Just one sheet of ice. You couldn't hardly walk. You couldn't hardly walk. Now someone this way, someone the other way. There was no more order."},{"start":2821.0,"end":2825.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Everybody worked this way and we just walked ahead and walked ahead."},{"start":2826.0,"end":2833.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Now by evening I was so tired and could so hurt my,"},{"start":2833.0,"end":2837.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"it hurt so much my legs hurt so much that I had"}],"b":[{"start":11.0,"end":12.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Go on, should I tell?"},{"start":13.0,"end":34.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Yeah but my legs were very tired then. But I fell on the side of the road and there I laid for I don't know how long, an hour or two maybe, till somebody woke me up. And I looked up and there was a guy with me and says \"come on, come on, you cannot stay here, you have to [go]!\""},{"start":34.0,"end":45.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I said, \"I cannot walk no more\". And then he said, \"all right\". He took me in, put me up the wagon. And that was a bread wagon. They had nothing but a whole wagon load of bread."},{"start":46.0,"end":51.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And so we got on. and I dont know how long we was riding that night."},{"start":51.0,"end":52.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was evening,"},{"start":52.0,"end":53.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"it was late at night and dark."},{"start":54.0,"end":59.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So we come to a little farm, and there was the rest of the fellas. They were still already too."},{"start":59.0,"end":60.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Some of them was"},{"start":61.0,"end":64.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"in bed and some of them was still up."},{"start":65.0,"end":72.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And then I went to bed. though the fellow of the truck, from the wagon,"},{"start":73.0,"end":76.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"he says, \"go ahead now and here is a loaf of bread\"."},{"start":76.0,"end":77.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And he gave me a loaf of bread."},{"start":77.0,"end":79.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So he couldn't do nothing better! (he laughs quite hard)"},{"start":82.0,"end":84.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And then the next morning,"},{"start":84.0,"end":85.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"there was..."},{"start":87.0,"end":99.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The lieutenant came along and checked all the things and says, \"now we are all together and who has anything to eat yet?\""},{"start":99.0,"end":102.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Then he says, \"did you eat the iron ration?\""},{"start":103.0,"end":107.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"That's what he called it: 'iron ration'. \"You eat that without permission,"},{"start":107.0,"end":109.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"so you have to get punished for that.\""},{"start":109.0,"end":114.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So you know, the punishment was exercising in the snow,"},{"start":114.0,"end":118.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"up and down, down and up and up and down for a half an hour."},{"start":119.0,"end":122.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Because we eat the iron ration and nothing else to eat."},{"start":126.0,"end":128.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And after that we"},{"start":129.0,"end":135.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"can march into the front. It was was always \"front front front."},{"start":135.0,"end":145.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"To the front.\" We hear the shooting but the walking was so bad that we had not much progress that day."},{"start":148.0,"end":154.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And each time when we hit the a farm that was big enough for the company,"},{"start":155.0,"end":163.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So we stopped and lay down and rested a while till the officers came and say,"},{"start":164.0,"end":165.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"\"March\" and on, all,"},{"start":168.0,"end":170.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"We dragged alone and dragged along."},{"start":171.0,"end":179.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"But no kitchen. The kitchen couldn't come along because she she broke down all the time. I don't know why, but it always broke down."},{"start":180.0,"end":187.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So we had a terrible time getting the food, getting the food for us in the front."},{"start":192.0,"end":202.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Officers, they had a, he had a horse, he could go, he could sit on the horse with a big fur coat and he didn't feel the cold like we did,"},{"start":202.0,"end":205.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"but we all went along,"},{"start":205.0,"end":206.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"everybody was"},{"start":208.0,"end":217.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"willing to go, I suppose, I dunno. I was not exactly willing, but I went with a with a uh with your own with a heart when it has. There was not uh uh uh"},{"start":220.0,"end":228.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So we made it straight so in the winter we was living then in a barn and we dig some trenches for the winter."},{"start":230.0,"end":238.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And there was not much action, no, no action at all. Just working in the bag (possibly \"back\" referring to rear of the front line) and doing [stuff]. But then when the spring came and the"},{"start":240.0,"end":251.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"the corn thawed off out, then we had to dig trenches again. Then we did took some trenches, strange as I don't know what, we had three rows of trenches there."},{"start":254.0,"end":256.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And now on one day,"},{"start":256.0,"end":257.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"one day there comes the"},{"start":258.0,"end":264.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The water, to run we're going to go, you can straight down to Galicia."},{"start":265.0,"end":270.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The snow was gone already at that time, but it was an awful mess marching in that."},{"start":270.0,"end":276.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The water didn't go in the ground because the ground was frozen underneath and there was just mush."},{"start":276.0,"end":277.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was terrible."},{"start":278.0,"end":282.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Sometimes it runs up in your boots and not in your boots."},{"start":283.0,"end":294.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So we went down to Galicia and there was the office (pronounced \"off-ence-ceene\") Brusilov. Brusilov I think was the guy's name from the Russians."},{"start":294.0,"end":307.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He had a big offensive in Galicia, he wanted to get into Germany through Austria there, Galicia from the south."},{"start":307.0,"end":317.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So they said told us, but we've got to stop them. But we didn't. We did talk, yeah, but I don't know if we stopped them. I wasn't I wasn't there to finish the thing."},{"start":318.0,"end":321.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Because I got wounded then there on one night and"},{"start":323.0,"end":330.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"when I was laying there in apple orchard waiting for uh for our meal to come and..."},{"start":332.0,"end":334.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I got wounded and into"},{"start":336.0,"end":340.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"What happened before? is it's all drivers the same thing,"},{"start":340.0,"end":348.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"marching on nothing to eat, not allowed to drink the water because the water was poisoned by some [indecipherable]\\,"},{"start":348.0,"end":350.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"but we drank the water anyway,"},{"start":350.0,"end":352.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"even I didn't see nobody die."},{"start":353.0,"end":359.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"We all had good health, we didn't die from that water. The water was good I think."},{"start":364.0,"end":366.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"When I came to the hospital,"},{"start":367.0,"end":373.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"the doctor didn't examine me much. They just looked at you, they looked at you, they made some questions,"},{"start":373.0,"end":377.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"they put you to bed.  they [didnt] give you a bed, you have to go to bed yourself."},{"start":377.0,"end":388.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They give you a bed there, a cot, and you have to lay there for two days. Then one day the doctor came and he looked at me and..."},{"start":390.0,"end":409.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Give some orders to the guy that has, he must read them in the book and give them some orders and then that evening they came and put a badge on my chest, tied the badge on me and then the next day we went into the railroad car and up to Germany."},{"start":410.0,"end":414.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Northern Germany was that, Marienburg."},{"start":415.0,"end":417.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was a nice hospital there and"},{"start":419.0,"end":440.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"all Sisters, Catholic Sisters, where they took good care, pretty good care. For the eats was very nice, not too much, but we [indecipherable]. That hospital had a big, big farm there. They had men working there and he had something to eat there, you know, they didn't depend on the on the far on the market."},{"start":441.0,"end":443.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So much. They had lots of food themselves."},{"start":445.0,"end":459.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Well, they took lots of course not satisfied with them. Like everybody is always grumbling, they want more and more. We didn't eat -- we didn't live there for to get fat, we had to eat to keep living, eh?"},{"start":462.0,"end":467.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And the fact that that exam we have after two days."},{"start":468.0,"end":470.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He was very nice. He was, say,"},{"start":470.0,"end":473.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"a countryman of mine, from my church."},{"start":474.0,"end":484.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He was banned over there because he didn't like, he had, he said something about the Germans, and they banned him up there. They took him away from us and sent him up there in hospital."},{"start":485.0,"end":486.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So he said."},{"start":491.0,"end":493.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I was happy to be there."},{"start":495.0,"end":499.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"But there's the the flu was at that time."},{"start":500.0,"end":504.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And there was so many people died in that hospital from the flu."},{"start":507.0,"end":515.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"What happened? I don't know. Does the flu we heard that what kind of Asian flu they got they called it."},{"start":516.0,"end":519.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And the people got sick and then there was uh"},{"start":520.0,"end":522.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"You had the fever."},{"start":522.0,"end":523.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"they got a fever."},{"start":524.0,"end":532.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So they bandaged him up all over the whole body bandaged him up and make him sweat."},{"start":533.0,"end":535.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Now if it helps? what help I don't know."},{"start":539.0,"end":544.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"When you're young you don't pay much attention. you look [out] for yourself a little bit and that's all right."},{"start":545.0,"end":550.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"There was all kinds of rigmarole with the Germans and the Alsatians."},{"start":551.0,"end":556.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They always asked where you come from and when they hear you was an Alsatian."},{"start":557.0,"end":558.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So you was a half enemy,"},{"start":559.0,"end":561.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"you know? you was not a real German anymore."},{"start":561.0,"end":569.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"You was half enemy but that didn't bother me too much. I didn't say nothing to them, I left them alone."},{"start":572.0,"end":586.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"My well-date came, and the doctor called me just now. you have already just think what I said. Don't let them operate on you. You have all right to intervene as you need it. You will operate if you don't let them, let's see that."},{"start":587.0,"end":591.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I went home and I was sent home to the regiment."},{"start":593.0,"end":606.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The Recuporation Company, what they call recuperation, they told you guys recuperate there the village, had nothing to do, just lay around and go around the town and come home for eat."},{"start":607.0,"end":611.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"coffee in the morning, cold"},{"start":612.0,"end":617.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"most of the time, of course. there was no time, nobody was bought in time, nobody got it in time or brought in time."},{"start":618.0,"end":624.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And then for lunch we get some kind of a stew with lots of turnips in it."},{"start":625.0,"end":627.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And if you get a piece of meat,"},{"start":628.0,"end":628.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"that's lucky."},{"start":628.0,"end":633.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"If there was no piece of meat in the dish,"},{"start":633.0,"end":634.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"you get none."},{"start":634.0,"end":634.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"You just must."},{"start":635.0,"end":639.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And then one piece of bread was the pumpernickel,"},{"start":639.0,"end":641.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"what they call the Germans the pumpernickel."},{"start":642.0,"end":643.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was divided in three."},{"start":644.0,"end":645.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And, I mean,"},{"start":645.0,"end":649.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"\"Jacques just showed that every piece was equal\","},{"start":649.0,"end":650.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"you know."},{"start":651.0,"end":653.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Three men get one pumpernickel."},{"start":656.0,"end":664.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"During the evening, there was coffee or tea and a piece of cheese sometimes,"},{"start":665.0,"end":667.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"sometimes a piece of herring."},{"start":668.0,"end":672.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And if you had a piece of bread left from the pumpernickel,"},{"start":672.0,"end":673.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"alright,"},{"start":673.0,"end":676.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"with the nuts you had to drink your tea without bread."},{"start":680.0,"end":681.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So the city, if you had money,"},{"start":681.0,"end":685.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"you could buy something in the city. that's alright, if you had money."},{"start":686.0,"end":693.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"But state, the state marks (deutschmark?) we got every ten days was not going too far."},{"start":694.0,"end":705.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Yeah, that's not part of us, yeah. Once in a while you give the picture, you give a piece of cake or a piece of bread, you know, that's to treat how you feel like it."},{"start":710.0,"end":713.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"One day there is the bread that broke out, the German revolution."},{"start":715.0,"end":720.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Yeah, German revolution broke out and that's what starts the end of the war with them."},{"start":720.0,"end":723.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I was still in the recuperation company."},{"start":725.0,"end":734.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Then the order came that the Alsatian has to go separated from the Germans and they have to go home."},{"start":735.0,"end":739.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They are let go free, they go home now, they get here free, they go home."},{"start":740.0,"end":743.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And they go to Strasbourg. that way they, don't put it on the show."},{"start":746.0,"end":761.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I worked in Strasbourg and was very happy with my job and everything else, but there came so many tourists and I should have [spoke] more French and more English."},{"start":762.0,"end":766.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"My French was not so good because we were not allowed to speak French in Alsace."},{"start":767.0,"end":771.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I went back to Paris and get a job in Paris."},{"start":772.0,"end":775.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And I worked there in Paris."},{"start":778.0,"end":779.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was a nice little hotel."},{"start":779.0,"end":797.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The [folks] was nice, everybody was nice, but I didn't speak English. In Paris then there was only English or French or Americans, I didn't know which it was. They all spoke the same \"aye, aye, aye\"."},{"start":798.0,"end":804.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And so I decided to go to this country, come to America to learn English."},{"start":812.0,"end":816.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And the American[s] convent to the American, they're all good men."},{"start":822.0,"end":829.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Contrary to my daddy saying, \"you cannot go to America because you was in the German army and they would let you in the America.\""},{"start":830.0,"end":831.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I said, \"oh no,"},{"start":831.0,"end":832.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I believe in God.\""},{"start":832.0,"end":848.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I went to the American council and told them the story. \"I want the American to learn English because I need it in my job here.\""},{"start":849.0,"end":850.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And the council,"},{"start":850.0,"end":855.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"he gave me the visa the same day as I was made the application."},{"start":856.0,"end":868.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And so then I wrote, then \"I had a cousin, a second cousin in Paris where he had relatives in the United States."},{"start":869.0,"end":871.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Their name was Bergmeyer.\""},{"start":871.0,"end":873.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And so she wrote."},{"start":874.0,"end":878.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"To put it to Mrs. and Mr. Bergmeyer"},{"start":878.0,"end":882.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and they sent me the affidavit."},{"start":884.0,"end":897.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They didn't take long at all. A couple of weeks and I had an affidavit. When I had the affidavit I went back to the American Council and showed the affidavit and I get my visa to go to America."},{"start":897.0,"end":899.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And so when I came to America"},{"start":900.0,"end":904.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I had a friend: a colleague was working with me in Paris."},{"start":905.0,"end":921.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He was a chef and he was here before. and I wrote to him and he said he wrote me back, [saying] this what I should do. I should come [to America] and he said he saw the ship to pick me up."},{"start":921.0,"end":923.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And if he's not [at] the ship,"},{"start":923.0,"end":927.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I should take a taxi and go to the address we were living."},{"start":928.0,"end":944.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I had and just as it happened he had a work and he was not on the ship so I took a taxi and gave him the address and they drove me to the boarding house,"},{"start":944.0,"end":951.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"a rooming house inbetween 49th Street between 2nd and 3rd Avenue."},{"start":952.0,"end":960.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And that was three English single women, single ladies they have there,"},{"start":961.0,"end":963.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"that rooming house."},{"start":964.0,"end":974.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And I rang the bell and she came down and she said, \"alright wait\", she said alright or something like that, I don't know exactly what she said."},{"start":975.0,"end":978.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And she went to the taxi to pay the taxi."},{"start":979.0,"end":982.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"On the taxi that I had [taken]. later on,"},{"start":982.0,"end":988.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"he asked seven dollars and she did give him hell. She hollered with him, she,"},{"start":988.0,"end":994.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I don't know what all it was said and then she gave him three dollars when the taxi left."},{"start":994.0,"end":997.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"She threatened them to be the police or something like that."},{"start":998.0,"end":1006.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Then from then on, then she put me in a room and my friend came in the evening after he was finished work."},{"start":1006.0,"end":1010.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And we had a good laugh about the taxi."},{"start":1013.0,"end":1016.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And next day, right away,"},{"start":1016.0,"end":1018.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I was hunting for a job."},{"start":1019.0,"end":1022.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And next day, you know what it was?"},{"start":1022.0,"end":1024.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The 17th of March."},{"start":1025.0,"end":1029.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I went hunting. I went across the city."},{"start":1032.0,"end":1038.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"There was a chap in the in the paper, one the front my friend had in uh"},{"start":1039.0,"end":1057.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"in each the west side of Broadway. And he told me how to get here. The streets are as if you go across Broadway and uh and then by around Times Square. Well I think it was forty sixth or forty seven street, Times Square there. When I get there, I want to go across."},{"start":1058.0,"end":1065.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Now that when I got to the fifth Avenue, when I come to the fifth Avenue there was the Irish"},{"start":1067.0,"end":1068.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Parade,"},{"start":1069.0,"end":1069.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"St."},{"start":1069.0,"end":1082.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Patrick's Parade. and I couldn't get across for two hours. So when I could get across and I come by 46th street and 47th street west of"},{"start":1083.0,"end":1092.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"broadway, the guy says \"the job is taken. Too late\", so I had to hunt for another one."},{"start":1093.0,"end":1097.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"But I took about two weeks before I get a job in Park Avenue,"},{"start":1099.0,"end":1101.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"375 Park Avenue."},{"start":1102.0,"end":1108.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"That's very nice job, that was a busboy job, I could do the busboy, I know about..."},{"start":1109.0,"end":1118.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"From, as I said, in France, you know, you... I taught to speak the French and the German. There was lots of German waiters, Austrians,"},{"start":1118.0,"end":1125.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Italians, and we get along pretty good there with the bosses. The boss was Austrian."},{"start":1125.0,"end":1127.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Two Austrian ladies have a restaurant."},{"start":1129.0,"end":1131.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And I worked there for two years."},{"start":1133.0,"end":1134.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The first..."},{"start":1135.0,"end":1140.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"year I got sick, I had a hemorrhage. I hemorrhaged"},{"start":1140.0,"end":1148.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"from the bullet or whatever it is, and they had to take me to the hospital in Wellfair Island,"},{"start":1149.0,"end":1152.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"wherever it is, Wellfair Island I think, it was in New York."},{"start":1153.0,"end":1159.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And in Wellfair Island there the doctor examined me and [undecipherable]"},{"start":1159.0,"end":1164.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They looked at the thing they were told about issue for the head and they decided,"},{"start":1165.0,"end":1167.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"\"oh yes, we've got to take that bullet out.\""},{"start":1168.0,"end":1168.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"\"Oh\", I said,"},{"start":1168.0,"end":1171.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"\"no you don't\". I said, \"no I will not\"."},{"start":1171.0,"end":1172.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"\"My doctor."},{"start":1173.0,"end":1183.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"That I had a doctor, I've been hospitalised, he (the doctor) says, it's not necessary because it's very well nicely healed when you shouldn't, shouldn't have it taken out.\""},{"start":1183.0,"end":1184.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Where was the hemorrhage?"},{"start":1184.0,"end":1186.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"In Wellfair Island in New York"},{"start":1186.0,"end":1187.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Where"},{"start":1187.0,"end":1187.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"City."},{"start":1187.0,"end":1188.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"was the haemorrhage?"},{"start":1189.0,"end":1190.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"How much I bled him,"},{"start":1190.0,"end":1190.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"You were coughing"},{"start":1190.0,"end":1191.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"out? Yeah."},{"start":1191.0,"end":1193.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"blood."},{"start":1193.0,"end":1202.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I spit the blood all out. It come out shot now like this."},{"start":1202.0,"end":1202.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"What did it feel like?"},{"start":1203.0,"end":1207.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Ah, it's heat, I could uh could it's terrible, you know, when you look about if the"},{"start":1207.0,"end":1208.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"But what's was it"},{"start":1208.0,"end":1208.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"our our"},{"start":1208.0,"end":1208.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"painful?"},{"start":1208.0,"end":1209.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"your stomach, huh? Was"},{"start":1209.0,"end":1209.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Was it"},{"start":1209.0,"end":1209.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"very"},{"start":1209.0,"end":1209.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"painful?"},{"start":1209.0,"end":1211.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"painful, I don't know."},{"start":1212.0,"end":1212.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It was painful."},{"start":1213.0,"end":1222.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was pain too, it it it uh hardly it hard light, you know, yeah yeah. So the uh did you shut off the sh it?"},{"start":1222.0,"end":1223.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"No."},{"start":1225.0,"end":1225.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Did you"},{"start":1225.0,"end":1225.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Yes."},{"start":1225.0,"end":1228.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"did you did they operate on"},{"start":1228.0,"end":1233.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"you? Well, no, I would take it up. They kept me there for another couple of days and then they let me go."},{"start":1233.0,"end":1235.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"How did they stop the haemorrhage?"},{"start":1236.0,"end":1236.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The hemorrhage stopped."},{"start":1237.0,"end":1238.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It stopped by itself?"},{"start":1238.0,"end":1241.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"By itself, yeah. The hemorrhage stopped by itself, yeah."},{"start":1243.0,"end":1244.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I think the hemorrhage"},{"start":1244.0,"end":1244.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Where"},{"start":1244.0,"end":1244.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"stopped by"},{"start":1244.0,"end":1246.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"were you when you coughed up the blood?"},{"start":1247.0,"end":1248.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I was in the first room."},{"start":1249.0,"end":1250.0,"speaker":"Speaker C","text":"In a furnished room?"},{"start":1250.0,"end":1255.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Yeah, it wasn't a furnished room. It was in in the furnished room when I got hemorrhage after work."},{"start":1255.0,"end":1255.0,"speaker":"Speaker C","text":"Oh, at home."},{"start":1255.0,"end":1268.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Home, yeah. In the the furnished after work. After work and the I coul I I knocked on the door. I knocked and hollered and then uh I was in the bathroom."},{"start":1268.0,"end":1273.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Blood came out of the sink and when the bulls come up from the flesh draw,"},{"start":1274.0,"end":1277.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"then he come up and see that and he says,"},{"start":1277.0,"end":1280.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"oh my God, he cried and he called the ambulance, you know,"},{"start":1281.0,"end":1283.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"he pointed the wolf island there."},{"start":1284.0,"end":1287.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And I said, we can wait for island and everything was alright."},{"start":1288.0,"end":1290.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"When I come back to work,"},{"start":1290.0,"end":1291.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"the boss says,"},{"start":1291.0,"end":1293.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"sure you can come work next week again."},{"start":1295.0,"end":1297.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I had a job anyway by uh"},{"start":1297.0,"end":1298.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"What year was this?"},{"start":1298.0,"end":1298.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"hmm?"},{"start":1298.0,"end":1299.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"What year was it?"},{"start":1300.0,"end":1304.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Uh, 1923/1922"},{"start":1304.0,"end":1305.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"How old were you?"},{"start":1306.0,"end":1310.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I was 28/29. Yeah yeah."},{"start":1310.0,"end":1313.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"22 or 23 I had that"},{"start":1315.0,"end":1317.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"What was it, twenty five, stra um twenty three, twenty three,"},{"start":1317.0,"end":1319.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"twenties, many twenties here."},{"start":1331.0,"end":1333.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"No, it was not uh"},{"start":1335.0,"end":1345.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I suppose when you lose them all alone you know nobody and everything go to work in the morning and go home one night and that's all you know."},{"start":1346.0,"end":1348.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"That's a guy that you have nobody."},{"start":1353.0,"end":1356.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So Shadowbrook I don't know. But uh that Missus"},{"start":1357.0,"end":1369.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Bergmeyer. I went to Miss to see Mrs. Bergmeyer in Newark because she she had made she had directed that to me. Could I take out that? Could you let me put it back just for to save time."},{"start":1371.0,"end":1381.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Uh then I went to see Mrs. Bergmeyer in Newark. I took I asked to go uh the the direction where I can go, where the uh how the address was? And when I got out of the"},{"start":1382.0,"end":1382.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I"},{"start":1382.0,"end":1386.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"tube in Newark I get up in the street and"},{"start":1388.0,"end":1407.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"look around, there was a cop there somewhere and I went to him and I showed him the address that I want to go there and he says oh they take me to go all \"walk up there\" and I walked and walked and walked and oh god I could never find that things."},{"start":1407.0,"end":1408.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Sure, what's happened."},{"start":1410.0,"end":1417.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"You know, when you don't know the road, it's always harder. It takes so long, the road, you know, so far."},{"start":1418.0,"end":1421.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I made another couple up there, and I asked him, and I said,"},{"start":1421.0,"end":1422.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"that,"},{"start":1422.0,"end":1423.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"you ain't right,"},{"start":1423.0,"end":1431.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and she's going next to the next corner, you turn left and get the other street up there. And that's right up there that it is."},{"start":1431.0,"end":1449.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And so I went up there, and I found the number there in the house, and I feel a surprise, and she had a cup of tea or a cup of coffee, I don't know, and then I went home that evening, I went home and then I found the way home."},{"start":1450.0,"end":1454.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So she gave me the address of her sister."},{"start":1455.0,"end":1462.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"My assistance when my year is my last letter in the Bronx."},{"start":1464.0,"end":1477.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And she says now maybe when you have time you can go up there and receive that sort of idea that somebody you don't. So one day I went up there you know."},{"start":1478.0,"end":1482.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I was up there I received."},{"start":1483.0,"end":1486.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I go back to work and now"},{"start":1488.0,"end":1492.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"I was a year uh working by the uh"},{"start":1493.0,"end":1508.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"At Park avenue then the boss says now, [undecipherable] in the summer it's New York, the rest are very poor, the the rich people they all go out of the town. Uh you know the better people, you know."},{"start":1508.0,"end":1510.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And they said,"},{"start":1510.0,"end":1514.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"do we give everybody a VEGO? You can have a VEGO too."},{"start":1516.0,"end":1518.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And I had the VEGO."},{"start":1520.0,"end":1533.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Then I went to Newark and asked my aunt where I could go to, I have a VEGO, where I should go to where I'd be going,"},{"start":1533.0,"end":1534.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"which is a..."},{"start":1534.0,"end":1541.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"You can come to Belmar, you can come to Belmar, I mean Belmar for the summer."},{"start":1541.0,"end":1542.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"At Curtis Avenue."},{"start":1543.0,"end":1545.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Uh I stray mother."},{"start":1546.0,"end":1549.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"It's Al's grandmother's house, the one that Al and Anne have now."},{"start":1552.0,"end":1554.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Curtis Avenue in Belmar."},{"start":1555.0,"end":1561.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"But grandma had a bungalow across the street where I is living now"},{"start":1561.0,"end":1561.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Right."},{"start":1561.0,"end":1562.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"in Belmar."},{"start":1563.0,"end":1570.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"She had a bungalow there. And she says, you come for a week out there, that's all right, but that would be all right."},{"start":1570.0,"end":1571.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Was Al alive?"},{"start":1571.0,"end":1572.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Huh?"},{"start":1572.0,"end":1573.0,"speaker":"Speaker B","text":"Was Al alive?"},{"start":1574.0,"end":1578.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Yeah, Al was a baby."},{"start":1578.0,"end":1582.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He lived next to the grandma in Newark."},{"start":1583.0,"end":1590.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They had two houses right next to each other there and in one house there came Margaret and in the other house."},{"start":1591.0,"end":1595.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And the other brother was in the other house and that was where my sister lived there."},{"start":1596.0,"end":1608.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So I went to Belmar and when we was in Belmar then Shustin was working for the telephone company and she took a week off and she came down there too."},{"start":1608.0,"end":1609.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"She was down there too."},{"start":1610.0,"end":1620.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So we went to the beach, we can't run our love, so later on we go we go out in New York and we go to the movie once in a while, or go to the theatre. And uh"},{"start":1620.0,"end":1622.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"How was your English by that time?"},{"start":1622.0,"end":1630.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"uh well a little better. Uh a assistant she teach she coached me a little better the English yeah, but was"},{"start":1630.0,"end":1630.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Did she speak French?"},{"start":1630.0,"end":1631.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"that that's uh"},{"start":1631.0,"end":1632.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Did she speak French?"},{"start":1633.0,"end":1634.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"no, she"},{"start":1634.0,"end":1635.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Does she speak German?"},{"start":1636.0,"end":1646.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"She ought to talk German, yeah, because where we are living there in the Bronx, there is a, that was a German settlement."},{"start":1647.0,"end":1650.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They all were sitting with she, she below."},{"start":1651.0,"end":1651.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Hi Jenny."},{"start":1652.0,"end":1652.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Hi Jenny."},{"start":1653.0,"end":1653.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Hi!"},{"start":1655.0,"end":1659.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Uh and then she said, and then went out to be, went and after that."},{"start":1661.0,"end":1670.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"We made over in New York when I had my day off, which only your dad went round and took her out. She only worked in four o'clock, she worked from seven till three or till four, you know."},{"start":1672.0,"end":1673.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Or till two, I don't know."},{"start":1674.0,"end":1678.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"She had good hours, she worked for a telephone company, she had very good hours."},{"start":1678.0,"end":1681.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"But she was always off in the two o'clock or four."},{"start":1681.0,"end":1684.0,"speaker":"Speaker E","text":"I think having been together still."},{"start":1684.0,"end":1684.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Huh?"},{"start":1688.0,"end":1689.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I have to turn it a little bit."},{"start":1696.0,"end":1698.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Oh, it's Christ, we're closed."},{"start":1698.0,"end":1701.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Is it going, have you have to speak into it?"},{"start":1703.0,"end":1704.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Oh, you're going?"},{"start":1704.0,"end":1705.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Yep."},{"start":1711.0,"end":1720.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I'll tell you what, but later I don't now I want to tell you how my brother first finished his service in the army."},{"start":1722.0,"end":1730.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"My was drafted in the French army and served in the French army till the collapse of the French"},{"start":1732.0,"end":1733.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Republic. Then"},{"start":1735.0,"end":1736.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"he went home."},{"start":1739.0,"end":1746.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I stayed home about three months. Then Hitler took over Alsace again"},{"start":1747.0,"end":1748.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and"},{"start":1749.0,"end":1765.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"incorporated Alsace in the in the in the Westmark he called it. And then he took all the young men and put it and put them in the army. So Joseph was drafted in the German army."},{"start":1767.0,"end":1773.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He had a training in Hungary. We put an event to Hungary and the training came."},{"start":1776.0,"end":1784.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"After the training was over, he went in with the Germans in the invasion of Normandy."},{"start":1787.0,"end":1791.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And in Normandy uh when the invasion of Normandy came and"},{"start":1793.0,"end":1801.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Joseph saw that things were going to get bad there so"},{"start":1801.0,"end":1806.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He hide in a farmer's, he went in a farmer's home."},{"start":1807.0,"end":1812.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The farmer's was, there was nobody in the farm, no. everybody was gone."},{"start":1812.0,"end":1814.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And he hid in the cellar."},{"start":1816.0,"end":1817.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He was in the cellar"},{"start":1819.0,"end":1827.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"A day and then he finds an old clothes in the farm, farm's clothes,"},{"start":1827.0,"end":1831.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"so he took the uniform,"},{"start":1832.0,"end":1842.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"the German uniform, and buried it in the yard and went back in the cellar. So he was three days in the cellar."},{"start":1843.0,"end":1853.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"There was nothing to eat but outside. it would rain. There was cider, there were lots of barrels of cider, I'm telling you. So we had cider to drink."},{"start":1854.0,"end":1865.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Then the third day he was taken to a vehicle, went upstairs and looked around and he seen some English soldiers around there."},{"start":1865.0,"end":1870.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So he went to them and he told them what happened, where he was and what he was doing."},{"start":1872.0,"end":1876.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So the Englishman took him and"},{"start":1878.0,"end":1883.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"transferred him to England as a prisoner of war."},{"start":1883.0,"end":1889.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And it was a prisoner of war came in England and then the English"},{"start":1890.0,"end":1896.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"found out that he was an Alsatian and they sent him then"},{"start":1898.0,"end":1900.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"to a cave inside France."},{"start":1900.0,"end":1904.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He deferred to the Free French Army again with under de Gaulle."},{"start":1906.0,"end":1914.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"And then he became a French soldier again. And then he fought up the Rhône valley."},{"start":1915.0,"end":1917.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and went into the Rhine Valley,"},{"start":1917.0,"end":1928.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"didn't got into the Rhine above that, that wasn't, not, there are no big battles there, but he had some skirmishes with the Germans and"},{"start":1930.0,"end":1938.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"the war was then almost over. And so he was in the French army for a couple of months and"},{"start":1939.0,"end":1952.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"He sent him home again because he was needed home on the farm. My mother and my sister was alone on the farm and they needed him."},{"start":1970.0,"end":1979.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"I can imagine how frustrated it was after the mother and my sister was leaving me the cellar for two weeks."},{"start":1981.0,"end":1985.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They couldn't come out while that battle was going on in Strasbourg."},{"start":1990.0,"end":1992.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"It was heavy to see him."},{"start":2024.0,"end":2027.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"in camp I believe was a prisoner of war camp,"},{"start":2028.0,"end":2031.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and you know what's, who should, who's living in Camberly now, he's,"},{"start":2032.0,"end":2036.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"he, um, my son, Harry,"},{"start":2036.0,"end":2037.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"is living in Camberly now."},{"start":2062.0,"end":2063.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Tell me about the Nazis."},{"start":2063.0,"end":2063.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Hmm?"},{"start":2063.0,"end":2065.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Tell me about the Nazis in [indecipherable name]."},{"start":2066.0,"end":2068.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and uh during"},{"start":2071.0,"end":2089.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"the war I was a sailor and during the war in England there was a little French sympathiser and there was German sympathiser and there was always a silent battle going on."},{"start":2091.0,"end":2103.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"The people couldn't uh the people couldn't say nothing and of course I was afraid to talk because somebody might hear and here is like"},{"start":2107.0,"end":2117.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"we should we should my brother-in-law's brother he opened his mouth once and talked said something and"},{"start":2118.0,"end":2126.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Two days later, the Nazi Gestapo was there and took him with his wife and their daughter and put him in a concentration camp."},{"start":2128.0,"end":2135.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So then that went on and on and so it went on and on."},{"start":2137.0,"end":2140.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"So people were afraid to talk or anything."},{"start":2154.0,"end":2159.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"What was that town in [unknown name] that they burnt down? The town that they burnt down."},{"start":2162.0,"end":2165.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"What was the town that they burnt down?"},{"start":2165.0,"end":2166.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Burnt down?"},{"start":2168.0,"end":2171.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"Oh they all died. That was in south France."},{"start":2173.0,"end":2174.0,"speaker":"Speaker D","text":"Wasn't that Negele?"},{"start":2174.0,"end":2179.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"No that was not in Negele. No that was in South France where the um"},{"start":2181.0,"end":2187.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"They shot the whole village in South France"},{"start":2189.0,"end":2192.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and there was a misunderstanding"},{"start":2194.0,"end":2200.0,"speaker":"Speaker A","text":"and there was another village but almost with the same name. What was the name? Shadowburg."}]};
